   One notion is that "bad binding detection" can be the responsibility of
yet another middle tier process.  Why not a process that has a list of
servers that should be running.  All it does is "ping" them occasionally,
and take some appropriate action for ones that are down.  The appropriate
action could be email to a human, restarting the server, notifying the
clients, writing to some datafile, or whatever.

