one's other APIs as well as one would like.  (Of course they
participated in the Winsock design, so...)  But they have a pretty
reasonable track record here; consider the (what I thought to be the
amusingly named, considering the newsgroup we're in) get_osfhandle()
and open_osfhandle() calls that can be used to map between "file
descriptors" and "OS handles" (HANDLEs in the Win16 and Win32 APIs).
