There is another school that says that the namespace should accurately
reflect what is going on.  Inefficiencies should be fixed -- and over
time will be, if only by getting better hardware :-).

Yes a client must be able to handle outdated binding data that sends it
off to a non-existent server, but this should not be the common case.
Strive to optimize the common case.

I don't like disagreeing with Nat, but I guess I do here.  I also do not
think that most clients will be long-lived or that they will be talking to
many servers, and that client-side caches are therefore not very useful.
"It is agreed the ice is then here."
