Right.  I'll just offer a caution against designing a system based on
artifacts of the development environment and not the presumably more
important characteristics of the deployment environment.

: You can probalby solve most of the people with the following capabilities:
:     start server at boot time
:     start server when directed to do so
:     start server when it exits (non-zero)
:     start server when you have an operation request it should get

: Yes this isn't perfect, but it's more then just a baby-step.

I guess where I see things getting sticky is when you want to run more
than one instance of server of a particular sort on a single host.
E.g., one server per distinct client user identity or one server per
distinct "object" (or set of objects) being operated on.  
