Certainly servers of this sort will be around.  (Note that they also
happen to be ones that fall into the category of servers that are hard
to start automatically via a "dced" tool--how is the tool supposed to
know whether an already-running server instance is supporting the
transaction that the client wants.  Clearly there are ways to make
this work.  My only point is that a simple auto-start facility might
not be as useful as one would wish.)

In any case, I guess I wonder whether it's appropriate to export these
transient servers into the namespace.  I think I can equally well
(perhaps better) imagine a scheme where a "transaction starter" server
is cataloged in the name space and you contact it and it tells you
where the real server you want is.  Or something.  Not everything
needs to be in the namespace.  Application-specific rendezvous schemes
are bound to exist.

