Well it's probably that bad. OSF and UI seem to be both loosing ground after
the Novell coup. This was the political side. From a technical standpoint
OSF might have made the mistake to actually provide TECHNOLOGY. This in the
case of DME seems to be a pretty massive task that eventually might not
succeed. I think today X/Open is the hottest group when it comes to
DM-standardization. They currently try to settle APIs for all the aspects
connected with DM. This is much easier than acutally provide real
implementations of APIs, especially when this technology is beeing combined
from different sources. Looks like CORBA will play an important role in this
X/Open effort.

