In article <RWESSMAN.93Sep10093324@rwessman.us.oracle.com> rwessman@rwessman.us.oracle.com (Rick Wessman) writes:
>I'm having difficulty compiling an IDL file when including DCE include files.
>The IDL file (simplified) looks like this:
>
>#include <dce/nbase.h>
>#include <dce/id_base.h>
>
>.
>.
>.
>interface foobarif
>{
>    void foobar([out, ref] sec_id_pac_t  *pac);
>}
>
>When I run idl, I get:
>
>idl -v -cc_cmd "gcc -c -g" -keep all -I. -I/opt/dcelocal/share/include -I/usr/xpg2include foobar.idl
>Running C preprocessor /lib/cpp   foobar.idl -I. -I. -I/opt/dcelocal/share/include -I/usr/xpg2include -I/usr/include
>Importing IDL file /opt/dcelocal/share/include/dce/nbase.idl
>Running C preprocessor /lib/cpp   /opt/dcelocal/share/include/dce/nbase.idl -I. -I. -I/opt/dcelocal/share/include -I/usr/xpg2include -I/usr/include
>Warning: Semantic checking prevented by other reported errors
>idl: File /opt/dcelocal/share/include/dce/idlbase.h, line 160: typedef struct
>idl: Syntax error near "typedef"
>
>Compilation aborted
>
>Has anyone ever seen this before?
>
If you want to include other .idl files in your .idl file, the proper
syntax is to use the "import" command.

So, replace the #include with the following

	interface foo {

		import "dce/nbase.idl";
		import .....

	....
	}

Also, the nbase idl file is automatically included in the stub files
that are generated. Poke around the stub files and header file and you
will see that a lot of header files are included for you.

Jonathan
